Fix build: -Werror treats the plain #define of IEEE80211_HDRLEN here as
a hard error once rdk-wifi-libhostap is a DEPENDS (EasyMesh/em_extender
builds only - see ccsp-one-wifi.bbappend's
`DEPENDS += "...EasyMesh...rdk-wifi-libhostap..."`). Its installed
src/common/ieee802_11_defs.h already defines the same macro
(sizeof(struct ieee80211_hdr), 24 bytes for the non-QoS/no-addr4 case -
same value, so this is a naming collision, not a behavior difference)
and gets pulled in transitively via the em apps-manager include chain
(wifi_apps_mgr.h -> wifi_ctrl.h -> wifi_mgr.h -> wifi_monitor.c). Guard
with #ifndef so whichever header is seen first wins, instead of
redefining unconditionally.

---
 source/apps/em/wifi_em.h | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/source/apps/em/wifi_em.h b/source/apps/em/wifi_em.h
--- a/source/apps/em/wifi_em.h
+++ b/source/apps/em/wifi_em.h
@@ -39,7 +39,9 @@
 #define WIFI_EM_FAILED_CONNECTION             "Device.WiFi.EM.FailedConnection"

 #define WNM_CATEGORY               10
+#ifndef IEEE80211_HDRLEN
 #define IEEE80211_HDRLEN           24
+#endif
 #define IEEE80211_EID_NEIGHBOR     52
 #define IEEE80211_NEIGHBOR_REPORT_MIN_LEN  13

